   "subject": "Changing branch length of outgroup",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello all, <div><br></div><div>When I plot some data using ggtree, the out groups are on a very long branch length. The out groups are 75 and 76 in the example below. </div><div><br></div><div>I would like to keep the out groups in the tree but ignore their branch lengths to make presentation easier.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-1WNmjsJgm-w/Worvy9UJzSI/AAAAAAAAAXs/Ny1zly0SsWYNB47fP3XhqhoQxDTUqrxhACLcBGAs/s1600/Rplot1.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-1WNmjsJgm-w/Worvy9UJzSI/AAAAAAAAAXs/Ny1zly0SsWYNB47fP3XhqhoQxDTUqrxhACLcBGAs/s1600/Rplot1.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482601222000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2bZCYzP0wKKZs2Pl7oYCPR\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-1WNmjsJgm-w/Worvy9UJzSI/AAAAAAAAAXs/Ny1zly0SsWYNB47fP3XhqhoQxDTUqrxhACLcBGAs/s1600/Rplot1.png\" border=\"0\"></a></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\">When I collapse the nodes 75 and 76 it does improve the appearance. but the out groups are still on a long branch.</p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-ij4rRSh_KhM/WorwQerho8I/AAAAAAAAAXw/RmYYtMRhfWMLMbyZQ7QMjCpSC2HSHaRQACLcBGAs/s1600/Rplot2.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-ij4rRSh_KhM/WorwQerho8I/AAAAAAAAAXw/RmYYtMRhfWMLMbyZQ7QMjCpSC2HSHaRQACLcBGAs/s1600/Rplot2.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482601222000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1GRzpAVjkgfj4gY0SzaBb7\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-ij4rRSh_KhM/WorwQerho8I/AAAAAAAAAXw/RmYYtMRhfWMLMbyZQ7QMjCpSC2HSHaRQACLcBGAs/s1600/Rplot2.png\" border=\"0\"></a></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\">Is it possible to produce a plot such as the one I created manually below where the branch lengths for the out groups is ignored </p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-64ekmkrEsB8/WorwjlCDTNI/AAAAAAAAAX4/h6AJpRRvlis18Qt-OAryamXB4dRfYnZsQCLcBGAs/s1600/Rplot3.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-64ekmkrEsB8/WorwjlCDTNI/AAAAAAAAAX4/h6AJpRRvlis18Qt-OAryamXB4dRfYnZsQCLcBGAs/s1600/Rplot3.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482601222000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2hWsWGcDXOrvlmqo79uB9l\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-64ekmkrEsB8/WorwjlCDTNI/AAAAAAAAAX4/h6AJpRRvlis18Qt-OAryamXB4dRfYnZsQCLcBGAs/s1600/Rplot3.png\" border=\"0\"></a></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><br></p><div>The script I have used so far is below and example data attached. Any thoughts would be much appreciated</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers</div><div>Ollie</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><div>library(ggtree)</div><div><br></div><div># read in data</div><div>x &lt;- read.tree(&quot;long-branch-example.newick&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div># create ggtree object</div><div>tree &lt;- ggtree(x) + geom_tiplab(size = 2)</div><div><br></div><div># plot tree</div><div>tree</div><div><br></div><div># find node for outgroup</div><div>MRCA(x, tip =c(&quot;75&quot;, &quot;76&quot;))</div><div><br></div><div># collapse outgroup node</div><div>tree &lt;- collapse(tree, node = 151)</div><div><br></div><div># plot resulting tree</div><div>tree</div></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
