    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Sorry for typo. pls use the following code:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;overflow-x:auto;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,248) none repeat scroll 0% 0%\"></code></pre></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;overflow-x:auto;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,248) none repeat scroll 0% 0%\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">library</span>(ggtree)\r\nx &lt;- read.tree(<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;long-branch-example.newick&quot;</span>)\r\ngroupClade(x, <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">151</span>) -&gt; y\r\nggtree(y, aes(linetype=group)) + geom_tiplab(size = <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">2</span></code></pre></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;overflow-x:auto;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,248) none repeat scroll 0% 0%\">) -&gt; p\r\np$data[p$data$node %<span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">in</span>% c(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">75</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">76</span>), <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;x&quot;</span>] = mean(p$data$x)\r\nprint(p)\r\n</code></pre>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:U29ycnkgZm9yIHR5cG8uIHBscyB1c2UgdGhlIGZvbGxvd2luZyBjb2RlOjxicj48YnI+YGBgcjxi\r\ncj5saWJyYXJ5KGdndHJlZSk8YnI+eCAmbHQ7LSByZWFkLnRyZWUoImxvbmctYnJhbmNoLWV4YW1w\r\nbGUubmV3aWNrIik8YnI+Z3JvdXBDbGFkZSh4LCAxNTEpIC0mZ3Q7IHk8YnI+Z2d0cmVlKHksIGFl\r\ncyhsaW5ldHlwZT1ncm91cCkpICsgZ2VvbV90aXBsYWIoc2l6ZSA9IDIpIC0mZ3Q7IHA8YnI+cCRk\r\nYXRhW3AkZGF0YSRub2RlICVpbiUgYyg3NSwgNzYpLCAieCJdID0gbWVhbihwJGRhdGEkeCk8YnI+\r\ncHJpbnQocCk8YnI+YGBgPGJyPjxicj48YnI+\" style=\"min-height:0;width:0;max-height:0;max-width:0;overflow:hidden;font-size:0em;padding:0;margin:0\">​</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Feb 23, 2018 at 6:28 PM, Yu, Guangchuang <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">gc...@connect.hku.hk</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">You can use <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">groupClade</code> to group the <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">151</code> clade and use that info to set the linetype. For shortening <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">75</code> and <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">76</code>, you can <em>manipulate</em> their <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">x</code> position.</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important\">library(ggtree)\r\nx &lt;- read.tree(&quot;long-branch-example.newick&quot;)\r\ngroupClade(x, 151) -&gt; y\r\nggtree(y, aes(linetype=group)) + geom_tiplab(size = 2) -&gt; p\r\np$data[tree$data$node %in% c(75, 76), &quot;x&quot;] = mean(p$data$x)\r\nprint(p)\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/bioc-ggtree/attach/17293500998b0/outgroup.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"Inline image 1\" width=\"351\" height=\"527\"></p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:PGRpdj48YnI+PGJyPjwvZGl2PllvdSBjYW4gdXNlIGBncm91cENsYWRlYCB0byBncm91cCB0aGUg\r\nYDE1MWAgY2xhZGUgYW5kIHVzZSB0aGF0IGluZm8gdG8gc2V0IHRoZSBsaW5ldHlwZS4gRm9yIHNo\r\nb3J0ZW5pbmcgYDc1YCBhbmQgYDc2YCwgeW91IGNhbiAqbWFuaXB1bGF0ZSogdGhlaXIgYHhgIHBv\r\nc2l0aW9uLjxicj48YnI+PGJyPjxkaXY+PGRpdj5gYGA8YnI+bGlicmFyeShnZ3RyZWUpPGJyPngg\r\nJmx0Oy0gcmVhZC50cmVlKCJsb25nLWJyYW5jaC1leGFtcGxlLm5ld2ljayIpPGJyPmdyb3VwQ2xh\r\nZGUoeCwgMTUxKSAtJmd0OyB5PGJyPmdndHJlZSh5LCBhZXMobGluZXR5cGU9Z3JvdXApKSArIGdl\r\nb21fdGlwbGFiKHNpemUgPSAyKSAtJmd0OyBwPGJyPnAkZGF0YVt0cmVlJGRhdGEkbm9kZSAlaW4l\r\nIGMoNzUsIDc2KSwgIngiXSA9IG1lYW4ocCRkYXRhJHgpPGJyPnByaW50KHApPGJyPmBgYDxicj48\r\nYnI+PGltZyBzcmM9Imh0dHBzOi8vbWFpbC5nb29nbGUuY29tL21haWwvdS8wLz91aT0yJmFtcDtp\r\naz1kZDgyODU4MzY3JmFtcDt2aWV3PWZpbWcmYW1wO3RoPTE2MWMyMzMyY2RiMTI4OTUmYW1wO2F0\r\ndGlkPTAuMSZhbXA7ZGlzcD1lbWImYW1wO3JlYWxhdHRpZD1paV8xNjFjMjMzMmNkYjEyODk1JmFt\r\ncDthdHRiaWQ9QU5HamRKOW5tdzI0aHJZRW5iTmw0MW0zdUdpR1R0R2RDXzhTejlrUzAzcUhoZi1z\r\nV3NOVmtkQnEwSklkMVZiOGxjWE9xcVdiQVM2Tl9pQTZlVzhyOGFVS0VvM1NkOUtxTElWdHJOY2oz\r\nRHZuYzJqMkpjMnlKUXpEeGpGdjdROCZhbXA7c3o9czAtbDc1JmFtcDthdHM9MTUxOTM4MTU4OTgw\r\nMyZhbXA7cm09MTYxYzIzMzJjZGIxMjg5NSZhbXA7enciIGRhdGEtc3VybD0iaHR0cHM6Ly9tYWls\r\nLmdvb2dsZS5jb20vbWFpbC91LzAvP3VpPTImYW1wO2lrPWRkODI4NTgzNjcmYW1wO3ZpZXc9Zmlt\r\nZyZhbXA7dGg9MTYxYzIzNTNkMjgwMzcwNyZhbXA7YXR0aWQ9MC4xJmFtcDtkaXNwPWVtYiZhbXA7\r\ncmVhbGF0dGlkPWlpXzE2MWMyMzMyY2RiMTI4OTUmYW1wO2F0dGJpZD1BTkdqZEpfbVNxUnhTcUl6\r\nczFVMXB6dmdJaEJKRVFDX0RXWkVNSW9jSEs1SkRWWF81YnUza0s0Y28ydEFma2N3M3JuQ2NOT01q\r\nZlFhejMxSUo1NDEydW5GUmVtNEg3OUpjdUloem9pZDJ6VUJPRWhCYWxjOTdHWUZvcU8yUTJrJmFt\r\ncDtzej1zMC1sNzUmYW1wO2F0cz0xNTE5MzgxNzI1MDAxJmFtcDtybT0xNjFjMjM1M2QyODAzNzA3\r\nJmFtcDt6dyIgYWx0PSJJbmxpbmUgaW1hZ2UgMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSI1MjciIHdpZHRoPSIzNTEiPjxi\r\ncj48L2Rpdj48L2Rpdj4=\" style=\"min-height:0;width:0;max-height:0;max-width:0;overflow:hidden;font-size:0em;padding:0;margin:0\">​</div></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Mon, Feb 19, 2018 at 11:50 PM, Ollie White <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">o.willi...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Apologies file attached now<div><div><br><br>On Monday, February 19, 2018 at 3:48:01 PM UTC, Ollie White wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello all, <div><br></div><div>When I plot some data using ggtree, the out groups are on a very long branch length. The out groups are 75 and 76 in the example below. </div><div><br></div><div>I would like to keep the out groups in the tree but ignore their branch lengths to make presentation easier.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-1WNmjsJgm-w/Worvy9UJzSI/AAAAAAAAAXs/Ny1zly0SsWYNB47fP3XhqhoQxDTUqrxhACLcBGAs/s1600/Rplot1.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-1WNmjsJgm-w/Worvy9UJzSI/AAAAAAAAAXs/Ny1zly0SsWYNB47fP3XhqhoQxDTUqrxhACLcBGAs/s1600/Rplot1.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482601236000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1O-ERy-AAnHStJWbl6tQgP\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-1WNmjsJgm-w/Worvy9UJzSI/AAAAAAAAAXs/Ny1zly0SsWYNB47fP3XhqhoQxDTUqrxhACLcBGAs/s1600/Rplot1.png\" border=\"0\"></a></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\">When I collapse the nodes 75 and 76 it does improve the appearance. but the out groups are still on a long branch.</p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-ij4rRSh_KhM/WorwQerho8I/AAAAAAAAAXw/RmYYtMRhfWMLMbyZQ7QMjCpSC2HSHaRQACLcBGAs/s1600/Rplot2.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-ij4rRSh_KhM/WorwQerho8I/AAAAAAAAAXw/RmYYtMRhfWMLMbyZQ7QMjCpSC2HSHaRQACLcBGAs/s1600/Rplot2.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482601236000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1R0l3NeHN_zsZwUuZFEL-O\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-ij4rRSh_KhM/WorwQerho8I/AAAAAAAAAXw/RmYYtMRhfWMLMbyZQ7QMjCpSC2HSHaRQACLcBGAs/s1600/Rplot2.png\" border=\"0\"></a></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\">Is it possible to produce a plot such as the one I created manually below where the branch lengths for the out groups is ignored </p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-64ekmkrEsB8/WorwjlCDTNI/AAAAAAAAAX4/h6AJpRRvlis18Qt-OAryamXB4dRfYnZsQCLcBGAs/s1600/Rplot3.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-64ekmkrEsB8/WorwjlCDTNI/AAAAAAAAAX4/h6AJpRRvlis18Qt-OAryamXB4dRfYnZsQCLcBGAs/s1600/Rplot3.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482601236000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0qGuH-jRQROUvlAQM8X3Bo\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-64ekmkrEsB8/WorwjlCDTNI/AAAAAAAAAX4/h6AJpRRvlis18Qt-OAryamXB4dRfYnZsQCLcBGAs/s1600/Rplot3.png\" border=\"0\"></a></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><br></p><div>The script I have used so far is below and example data attached. Any thoughts would be much appreciated</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers</div><div>Ollie</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><div>library(ggtree)</div><div><br></div><div># read in data</div><div>x &lt;- read.tree(&quot;long-branch-example.newick&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div># create ggtree object</div><div>tree &lt;- ggtree(x) + geom_tiplab(size = 2)</div><div><br></div><div># plot tree</div><div>tree</div><div><br></div><div># find node for outgroup</div><div>MRCA(x, tip =c(&quot;75&quot;, &quot;76&quot;))</div><div><br></div><div># collapse outgroup node</div><div>tree &lt;- collapse(tree, node = 151)</div><div><br></div><div># plot resulting tree</div><div>tree</div></div><div><br></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div><div><div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nG Yu, DK Smith, H Zhu, Y Guan, TTY Lam*. ggtree: an R package for visualization and annotation of phylogenetic trees with their covariates and other associated data, Methods in Ecology and Evolution, 2017, 8(1):28-36. doi:10.1111/2041-210X.12628<br>\r\n <br>\r\nHomepage: <a href=\"https://guangchuangyu.github.io/ggtree\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://guangchuangyu.github.io/ggtree&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482601236000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0wV-l-bcd_pUfrjYntG3Xo\">https://guangchuangyu.github.io/ggtree</a><br>\r\n--- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;ggtree&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">bioc-ggtree+unsubscribe@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">bioc-...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br></div></div>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/bioc-ggtree/ec55f9af-afd2-400f-9b85-f66a8b4253a9%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/bioc-ggtree/ec55f9af-afd2-400f-9b85-f66a8b4253a9%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482601237000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1nqMP30_Cx1uO4W6faYjbi\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/bioc-ggtree/ec55f9af-afd2-400f-9b85-f66a8b4253a9%40googlegroups.com</a>.<div><div><br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482601237000&amp;usg=AOvVaw09gH_Yn0R6F4Pu3_-6rI2R\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</div></div></blockquote></div><br><br clear=\"all\"><br></div></div><span><font color=\"#888888\">-- <br><div data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"font-family:arial;font-size:small\">--~--~---------~--~----~------------~-------~--~----~</span><br></div><div>Guangchuang Yu PhD<br></div><div>Postdoc researcher<br>State Key Laboratory of Emerging Infectious Diseases<br>School of Public Health<br>The University\r\n                           of Hong Kong</div><div>Hong Kong SAR, China<br></div><div>www: <a href=\"https://guangchuangyu.github.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://guangchuangyu.github.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482601237000&amp;usg=AOvVaw123hrwkIAmvpzqByE2mOsZ\">https://guangchuangyu.